<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 50 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 50 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 50 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    800 MLN    850 MLN    850 MLN    850 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    400 MLN    750 MLN    800 MLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    400 MLN*   350 MLN*   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE	    =	    -	     50 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
